AB  - This study aimed to investigate the effects of a neuro-nutraceutical formulation comprising selenium-enriched Spirulina platensis (Se-SP) on cognitive and behavioral impairments, cholinergic deficits, selenium deficiency, and oxidative stress induced by intracerebroventricular injection of streptozotocin (ICV-STZ). The antioxidant capacity of Se-SP was confirmed through DPPH assay, and its selenium content was quantified using ICP-MS analysis. Fifty male rats were randomly assigned to five groups. Oral administration of the neuro-nutraceutical formulation (50 mg/kg) began after ICV-STZ injection and continued for 21 days. Selenium levels, cholinergic function, oxidative stress markers, and cognitive performance were evaluated. The results demonstrated that Se-SP treatment prevented acetylcholine depletion by inhibiting acetylcholinesterase activity and significantly improved behavioral test performance. Furthermore, Se-SP enhanced the activity of the selenoenzyme glutathione peroxidase, protecting against brain selenium depletion. It also effectively reduced ICV-STZ-induced lipid peroxidation by boosting antioxidant defenses. These findings suggest that Se-SP, as an organic antioxidant supplement, holds promise for alleviating oxidative stress and cholinergic dysfunction, thereby mitigating cognitive impairment
